 227:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****      *** Callback registration ***
 228:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****      =============================================
 229:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****     [..]
 230:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****      The compilation flag USE_HAL_I2C_REGISTER_CALLBACKS when set to 1
 231:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****      allows the user to configure dynamically the driver callbacks.
 232:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****      Use Functions HAL_I2C_RegisterCallback() or HAL_I2C_RegisterAddrCallback()
 233:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****      to register an interrupt callback.
 234:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****     [..]
 235:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****      Function HAL_I2C_RegisterCallback() allows to register following callbacks:
 236:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****        (+) MasterTxCpltCallback : callback for Master transmission end of transfer.
 237:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****        (+) MasterRxCpltCallback : callback for Master reception end of transfer.
 238:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****        (+) SlaveTxCpltCallback  : callback for Slave transmission end of transfer.
 239:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****        (+) SlaveRxCpltCallback  : callback for Slave reception end of transfer.
 240:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****        (+) ListenCpltCallback   : callback for end of listen mode.
 241:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****        (+) MemTxCpltCallback    : callback for Memory transmission end of transfer.
 242:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****        (+) MemRxCpltCallback    : callback for Memory reception end of transfer.
 243:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****        (+) ErrorCallback        : callback for error detection.
 244:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****        (+) AbortCpltCallback    : callback for abort completion process.
 245:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****        (+) MspInitCallback      : callback for Msp Init.
 246:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****        (+) MspDeInitCallback    : callback for Msp DeInit.
 247:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****      This function takes as parameters the HAL peripheral handle, the Callback ID
 248:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****      and a pointer to the user callback function.
 249:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****     [..]
 250:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****      For specific callback AddrCallback use dedicated register callbacks : HAL_I2C_RegisterAddrCall
 251:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****     [..]
 252:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****      Use function HAL_I2C_UnRegisterCallback to reset a callback to the default
 253:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****      weak function.
 254:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****      HAL_I2C_UnRegisterCallback takes as parameters the HAL peripheral handle,
 255:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****      and the Callback ID.
 256:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****      This function allows to reset following callbacks:
 257:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****        (+) MasterTxCpltCallback : callback for Master transmission end of transfer.
 258:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****        (+) MasterRxCpltCallback : callback for Master reception end of transfer.
 259:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****        (+) SlaveTxCpltCallback  : callback for Slave transmission end of transfer.
 260:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****        (+) SlaveRxCpltCallback  : callback for Slave reception end of transfer.
ARM GAS  C:\Users\subdia\AppData\Local\Temp\cc5PSBSW.s 			page 6


 261:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****        (+) ListenCpltCallback   : callback for end of listen mode.
 262:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****        (+) MemTxCpltCallback    : callback for Memory transmission end of transfer.
 263:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****        (+) MemRxCpltCallback    : callback for Memory reception end of transfer.
 264:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****        (+) ErrorCallback        : callback for error detection.
 265:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****        (+) AbortCpltCallback    : callback for abort completion process.
 266:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****        (+) MspInitCallback      : callback for Msp Init.
 267:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****        (+) MspDeInitCallback    : callback for Msp DeInit.
 268:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****     [..]
 269:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****      For callback AddrCallback use dedicated register callbacks : HAL_I2C_UnRegisterAddrCallback().
 270:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****     [..]
 271:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****      By default, after the HAL_I2C_Init() and when the state is HAL_I2C_STATE_RESET
 272:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****      all callbacks are set to the corresponding weak functions:
 273:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****      examples HAL_I2C_MasterTxCpltCallback(), HAL_I2C_MasterRxCpltCallback().
 274:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****      Exception done for MspInit and MspDeInit functions that are
 275:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****      reset to the legacy weak functions in the HAL_I2C_Init()/ HAL_I2C_DeInit() only when
 276:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****      these callbacks are null (not registered beforehand).
 277:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****      If MspInit or MspDeInit are not null, the HAL_I2C_Init()/ HAL_I2C_DeInit()
 278:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****      keep and use the user MspInit/MspDeInit callbacks (registered beforehand) whatever the state.
 279:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****     [..]
 280:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****      Callbacks can be registered/unregistered in HAL_I2C_STATE_READY state only.
 281:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****      Exception done MspInit/MspDeInit functions that can be registered/unregistered
 282:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****      in HAL_I2C_STATE_READY or HAL_I2C_STATE_RESET state,
 283:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****      thus registered (user) MspInit/DeInit callbacks can be used during the Init/DeInit.
 284:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****      Then, the user first registers the MspInit/MspDeInit user callbacks
 285:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****      using HAL_I2C_RegisterCallback() before calling HAL_I2C_DeInit()
 286:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****      or HAL_I2C_Init() function.
 287:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****     [..]
 288:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****      When the compilation flag USE_HAL_I2C_REGISTER_CALLBACKS is set to 0 or
 289:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****      not defined, the callback registration feature is not available and all callbacks
 290:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****      are set to the corresponding weak functions.
 291:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c **** 
 292:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c **** 
 293:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****      *** I2C Workarounds linked to Silicon Limitation ***
 294:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****      ====================================================
 295:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****      [..]
 296:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****        Below the list of all silicon limitations implemented for HAL on STM32F1xx product.
 297:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****        (@) See ErrataSheet to know full silicon limitation list of your product.
 298:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c **** 
 299:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****        (+) Workarounds Implemented inside I2C HAL Driver
 300:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****           (++) Wrong data read into data register (Polling and Interrupt mode)
 301:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****           (++) Start cannot be generated after a misplaced Stop
 302:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****           (++) Some software events must be managed before the current byte is being transferred:
 303:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****                Workaround: Use DMA in general, except when the Master is receiving a single byte.
 304:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****                For Interrupt mode, I2C should have the highest priority in the application.
 305:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****           (++) Mismatch on the "Setup time for a repeated Start condition" timing parameter:
 306:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****                Workaround: Reduce the frequency down to 88 kHz or use the I2C Fast-mode if
 307:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****                supported by the slave.
 308:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****           (++) Data valid time (tVD;DAT) violated without the OVR flag being set:
 309:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****                Workaround: If the slave device allows it, use the clock stretching mechanism
 310:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****                by programming NoStretchMode = I2C_NOSTRETCH_DISABLE in HAL_I2C_Init.
