1000:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c **** 
1001:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****     (#) There are two modes of transfer:
1002:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****        (++) Blocking mode : The communication is performed in the polling mode.
1003:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****             The status of all data processing is returned by the same function
1004:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****             after finishing transfer.
1005:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****        (++) No-Blocking mode : The communication is performed using Interrupts
1006:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****             or DMA. These functions return the status of the transfer startup.
1007:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****             The end of the data processing will be indicated through the
1008:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****             dedicated I2C IRQ when using Interrupt mode or the DMA IRQ when
1009:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c ****             using DMA mode.
1010:Drivers/STM32F1xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f1xx_hal_i2c.c **** 
